# Menu path from launch to the oracle mission, for oracle_input.exe.
#
# PARTLY CALIBRATED. Seen so far (oracle/baseline/C_after_key, 2026-11-03): the main menu
# ("Select Game") is up 15 s after launch; it is a 640x480 screen centred in the 800x600 window.
# SINGLE PLAYER is at (237,232). The screens after it have not been seen: the game has crashed at
# start-up in every boot since (oracle/BASELINE.md, "After the CD key").
# Known: the game's window is class "SFC", title "Starfleet Command", 800x600 client area at the
# top-left of the Wine desktop (oracle_input "list", 2026-11-02). Coordinates are client pixels.
# The driver's "shot" is black under Wine (GDI cannot read the DirectDraw/GL surface): calibrate
# with ORACLE_SHOTS=10 oracle/run_oracle.sh <label>, which saves oracle/shot.sh captures of the Mac
# window, while that window is on the visible Space.
#
# Intended path (from the menu state names in StarFleetOP.exe: tState_Skirmish, SETUP_SKIRMISH):
#   main menu -> Skirmish -> mission list: "!Oracle Skirmish" (sorts first) -> Start/Launch
# The script fixes ships, sides, map and positions, so nothing on the setup screen matters.

window 120 Starfleet Command
sleep 15000

# --- main menu: SINGLE PLAYER
click 237 232
sleep 5000

# --- single player screen: Skirmish button
# click X Y
# sleep 5000

# --- skirmish screen: pick the first mission in the list, then start
# click X Y
# sleep 2000
# click X Y

# The game writes OracleTrace.txt once the mission has started.
waitfile 300 C:\Games\SFCOP\OracleTrace.txt
